{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nGerrit change 3191 (story 7a7a-ceb9-e9a5-4d8e) took `Verified -1` after a local `make verify` passed. All 4 CI pytest cells failed on `tests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability.py::test_no_test_addresses_a_bare_repository_by_discovery` (then named `..._heldout.py`), a true positive. That module is `pytest.mark.integration`.\n\nCI's gating `ubuntu-latest, py3.13` cell (`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml`, job `test`) runs TWO pytest steps: the default suite (`-m \"$DEFAULT_SUITE_MARKS\"`, which resolves to `not integration and not external` for this cell, `--dist worksteal`) and then the integration tier (`pytest -m integration --dist loadgroup --max-worker-restart=0`). `make test` runs only the first. `AGENTS.md` says `make test` \"selects exactly what CI's gating cell selects\", so an author who follows the contract can still be pushed red. Evidence, verbatim workflow text, and measurements are in this ticket's comments.\n\nThe parity guard `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py::test_repo_policy_nodes_run_only_in_the_existing_primary_cell` compares the workflow to a hard-coded constant and never reads the Makefile, so the drift was invisible. Bug 1035-bed7-c855-4732, which created `make verify`, stated the intent as \"complete by construction ... nothing can drift\"; it did not decide to exclude the integration step. So the fix restores parity.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **Makefile `test` recipe** gains a second pytest invocation after the existing one, mirroring CI's integration step: `pytest -m integration -n $(PYTEST_WORKERS) --dist loadgroup --max-worker-restart=0 -q`. The two run in sequence and `make` stops at the first failure, which matches CI (the integration step does not run when the default step fails). The existing default-tier line is unchanged. Update the `test` and `verify` help strings and recipe comments to say the target runs both tiers and to state the added cost (measured: 200 tests, ~4 min at `-n 4`).\n2. **Parity test** in `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` (extending the existing module, no new mechanism):\n   - A helper resolves, for a given `(os, python-version)` matrix cell, the ordered list of `(marker expression, --dist mode)` pairs run by every `pytest` step of the `test` job, resolving `-m \"$VAR\"` through the step's `env` matrix expression. It reuses the regex already used by `test_repo_policy_nodes_run_only_in_the_existing_primary_cell`; that test is refactored to call the shared helper with unchanged assertions.\n   - A helper parses the Makefile `test` recipe (via the existing `_make_recipe_bodies` / `_live_make_lines`) into the same `(marker expression, --dist mode)` list.\n   - `test_make_test_runs_exactly_the_gating_cells_pytest_selections`: the Makefile list equals the gating cell's list. Fails on the current tree (Makefile has 1 pair, CI has 2).\n   - `test_make_test_selection_is_a_superset_of_every_matrix_cell`: for every cell in the job's matrix (after `exclude`), every truth assignment over the marker names that appear in the expressions that the cell selects is also selected by some `make test` expression, evaluated with pytest's own `_pytest.mark.expression.Expression`. This makes the documented \"superset of every other matrix cell\" claim executable.\n   - A fixture-level negative check: the selection comparison fed a Makefile body without the integration line reports the missing `integration` selection (proves the guard can detect the 7a7a class without depending on the live tree).\n3. **Docs:** correct the `AGENTS.md` paragraph (the parenthetical, the \"superset\" clause, and the cost line) and `docs/local-dev-env.md`'s day-to-day gates block and cost paragraph to say `make test` runs the default tier and then the integration tier, matching the gating cell's two steps.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `Makefile` — `test` recipe second invocation; `test`/`verify` help text and comments.\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` — shared cell-selection helpers, refactor of the existing primary-cell test to use them, 3 new tests.\n- `AGENTS.md` — correct the `make test` / gating-cell claim and cost.\n- `docs/local-dev-env.md` — correct the gates block and cost paragraph.\n\nOut of scope: changing any CI workflow; other jobs in `_build-and-test.yml` (lint, pip-audit, sandbox-enforcement) that `make verify` already covers through `lint`/`typecheck` or that are separate lanes.\n\n## Testing\n\n- RED first: add the 3 new tests before editing the Makefile and record that `test_make_test_runs_exactly_the_gating_cells_pytest_selections` and the superset test fail on the unmodified Makefile; then GREEN after the Makefile change.\n- Targeted: `pytest tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py -q` passes (including the refactored primary-cell test).\n- Demonstration of AC5: in the worktree, temporarily add a test module that runs `git -C <bare repo>` (the 7a7a violation shape), run the `make test` integration-tier invocation exactly as the Makefile writes it, record that it fails on `test_no_test_addresses_a_bare_repository_by_discovery`, then delete the temporary module.\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass. `make verify` is not run in this session; Gerrit `Verified +1` is the full-suite check.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The actual marker selection used by CI's gating `ubuntu-latest, py3.13` cell is read from `.github/workflows/` and recorded verbatim on this ticket.\n- [x] `make test`'s selection and the gating cell's selection agree: `make test` runs `-m \"not integration and not external\" --dist worksteal` and then `-m integration --dist loadgroup --max-worker-restart=0`, matching the cell's two pytest steps.\n- [x] `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` asserts the Makefile `test` recipe's selections equal the gating cell's pytest selections and form a superset of every matrix cell; the equality test fails on the pre-fix Makefile.\n- [x] `AGENTS.md`'s claim is corrected to match the resolved contract, including the \"superset of every other matrix cell\" clause, and `docs/local-dev-env.md` agrees.\n- [x] Demonstrated: with the fix in place, a tree containing the 7a7a violation fails `make test`'s integration-tier invocation locally (and therefore `make verify`, which runs `test`).\n- [x] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass; the change lands with `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793538484858295001,"uuid":"d84b966c-9e52-4aa7-90bd-a998b20843e7"}